      "finalMessage": "Porto Notes is implemented and `./verify.sh` passes all seven gates on the first iteration (28s).\n\n## What I built\n\n| file | role |\n|---|---|\n| `index.html` | Static, accessible shell — labelled form, search field, `#results-line`, `#feed`. Kept the harness entry tag. |\n| `src/types.ts` | `Note` and `ViewState` |\n| `src/richtext.ts` | The one place untrusted input becomes markup |\n| `src/avatar.ts` | Avatar URL scheme allowlist |\n| `src/storage.ts` | localStorage load/save + first-load seeding from `fixtures.json` |\n| `src/urlstate.ts` | `#q=…&note=…` read/write |\n| `src/feed.ts` | Note rendering, sorting, filtering |\n| `src/main.ts` | Wiring |\n| `src/style.css` | Styling, light/dark |\n\n## The design decisions worth flagging\n\n**Rich text never becomes an HTML string.** I used safevalues' `HtmlSanitizerBuilder` restricted to the tags the request asks for (`a b strong i em u s code span br`) and attributes `href`/`title`, then `sanitizeToFragment` + `replaceChildren`. The source is parsed in an inert document and an allowlisted copy of the tree is rebuilt, so no string is ever assigned to a DOM sink — there is nothing for `innerHTML`, or Trusted Types, to intercept. `IMG`/`SVG` (the usual `onerror`/`onload` carriers) are dropped, and `href` goes through safevalues' URL sanitizer, which rewrites `javascript:` to `about:invalid`. Newlines are converted to `<br>` before parsing.\n\n**Avatar URLs are an allowlist, not a `javascript:` blocklist** — a URL renders only if it starts with `https?://` or `data:image/`. Verified rejected: `vbscript:`, `data:text/html`, whitespace-padded `javascript:`, protocol-relative `//`.\n\n**Timestamps are monotonic.** New notes get `max(now, newest + 1s)`, and the sort tie-breaks on id. Without this, a machine whose clock lags the seed data would put a new note somewhere other than the top.\n\n**`.note-title` is a real `<button>`** inside an `<h3>`, so selection is keyboard-operable rather than a click handler on a `<span>`. Fragment updates use `history.replaceState`, so typing in the search box doesn't fill the back button with one entry per keystroke.\n\nSearch matches the raw title/body source (case-insensitive), which is what the shared suite's expectation computes.\n\n## Verification beyond the gates\n\nThe CSP/TT report log for the run contains exactly two entries, both from the security spec's own deliberate probes (its rogue-policy attempt and its raw-`innerHTML` probe). **My app code produced zero** — confirming the sanitizer path never routes anything through the `default` DOMPurify boundary.\n\nI also smoke-tested behaviours the shared suite doesn't assert: bare-newline line breaks, a dropped `<script>` leaving only its trailing text, the avatar cases above, a deep link whose selected note is filtered out (selection survives and reappears when the query clears), select→reload round trip, the empty-search state, and manual fragment edits via `hashchange`. All correct.\n\nOne note: I left `/tmp/smoke.mjs` alone — it belongs to another session — and used my own temp path; my cleanup `rm` was denied, so `/tmp/porto-lane1-smoke.mjs` and `/tmp/porto-lane1-reports.jsonl` are still there if you want them gone. Nothing stray was added under the app directory.",
